                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "42fed67e-6a7d-4a48-b008-9102ddd1e662",
                        "entry_id": "8ee603f8-65df-388a-9c75-bf83c1e9eb92",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "предзнаменова́ниях"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "036d5148-25b3-3ae1-b07c-92678afcd89b",
                        "entry_id": "8ee603f8-65df-388a-9c75-bf83c1e9eb92",
                        "glosses": [
                            "примета, признак, указывающий на близость, скорое наступление чего-либо"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cf9b2eb8-252f-49ab-bc11-b97794babe79",
                                "sense_id": "036d5148-25b3-3ae1-b07c-92678afcd89b",
                                "text": "Навстречу Дубровскому попался поп со всем при́четом. Мысль о несчастливом предзнаменовании пришла ему в голову."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "af951507-014d-4b91-a141-82ab993ae82a",
                                "sense_id": "036d5148-25b3-3ae1-b07c-92678afcd89b",
                                "text": "Встреча с нею показалась ему особенно счастливым предзнаменованием; он обрадовался ей, словно родной."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "307ac338-f287-43b9-8d57-3268507c5d4d",
                                "sense_id": "036d5148-25b3-3ae1-b07c-92678afcd89b",
                                "text": "Скажу более: с каждым явлением его обыденной жизни в уме его была соединена какая-нибудь примета, какое-нибудь предзнаменование, делавшее его печальным или весёлым до тех пор, покуда новая примета не перевёртывала вверх дном все его соображения."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d05712fb-9c58-459c-85f5-755472f997bd",
                        "source_entry_id": "8ee603f8-65df-388a-9c75-bf83c1e9eb92",
                        "source_sense_id": "036d5148-25b3-3ae1-b07c-92678afcd89b",
                        "target_lang_word": "omen",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "omen",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "563c85ac-622b-3c94-ab4c-31bde1a9b0b5",
                                        "entry_id": "42643b0d-b6f3-3a68-b8fa-6a90fb66df3d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something which portends or is perceived to portend either a good or evil event or circumstance in the future, or which causes a foreboding; a portent or augury."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0fca03bc-a4b1-4a6c-965b-c726c960c407",
                                                "sense_id": "563c85ac-622b-3c94-ab4c-31bde1a9b0b5",
                                                "text": "The ghost's appearance was an ill omen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "025c89fa-ed08-4d4a-8de5-b659dec55c18",
                                                "sense_id": "563c85ac-622b-3c94-ab4c-31bde1a9b0b5",
                                                "text": "A rise in imports might be an omen of economic recovery."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "57b0181b-8e17-4f2a-9f97-da039889b8fd",
                                                "sense_id": "563c85ac-622b-3c94-ab4c-31bde1a9b0b5",
                                                "text": "The egg has, during the span of history, represented mystery, magic, medicine, food and omen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "458b748e-338c-49aa-b539-3aaf967552b9",
                                                "sense_id": "563c85ac-622b-3c94-ab4c-31bde1a9b0b5",
                                                "text": "Day broke. He saw three black hens asleep in a tree. He shuddered, horrified at this omen. Then he promised the Holy Virgin three chasubles for the church, and that he would go barefooted from the cemetery at Bertaux to the chapel of Vassonville."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "51faeb91-8f9d-3922-baaa-449dc2d460e3",
                                        "entry_id": "42643b0d-b6f3-3a68-b8fa-6a90fb66df3d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A thing of prophetic significance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba587f15-029e-428d-91c7-64a251856590",
                                                "sense_id": "51faeb91-8f9d-3922-baaa-449dc2d460e3",
                                                "text": "A sign of ill omen."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "omen",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8b320be9-e008-38f2-8552-6b9f797cba63",
                                        "entry_id": "6f6b40cc-4274-321a-8dd5-88660ea2e563",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To be an omen of."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a07d85ae-715f-3b59-be24-907eb683f3b6",
                                        "entry_id": "6f6b40cc-4274-321a-8dd5-88660ea2e563",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To divine or predict from omens."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b70ac893-20fb-48e8-867d-2c3e16fb2304",
                        "source_entry_id": "8ee603f8-65df-388a-9c75-bf83c1e9eb92",
                        "source_sense_id": "036d5148-25b3-3ae1-b07c-92678afcd89b",
                        "target_lang_word": "augury",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "augury",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "17bb9b8d-053b-3bfe-9cab-59cc856ea2b9",
                                        "entry_id": "66e7ea95-5214-3107-8a96-cbc4c4248925",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A divination based on the appearance and behaviour of animals."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "86800c1c-d4f3-344b-9239-08b66b82339b",
                                        "entry_id": "66e7ea95-5214-3107-8a96-cbc4c4248925",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An omen or prediction; a foreboding; a prophecy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "43a7c3c0-14bc-4c90-8263-a74db7ca1955",
                                                "sense_id": "86800c1c-d4f3-344b-9239-08b66b82339b",
                                                "text": "In Wordsworth's first preludings there is but a dim foreboding of the creator of an era. From Southey's early poems, a safer augury might have been drawn."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3679800a-3bf8-49c1-8d45-ffd5ce040274",
                                                "sense_id": "86800c1c-d4f3-344b-9239-08b66b82339b",
                                                "text": "No augury could be hopefuller. The Fates must indeed be hard, the Ordeal severe, the Destiny dark, that could destroy so bright a Spring!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d8eb4d7e-d9a1-49d4-8e7a-9dac4d0b916f",
                                                "sense_id": "86800c1c-d4f3-344b-9239-08b66b82339b",
                                                "text": "Fortunately many of the younger men are keen enough to make a success of their work, and this gives a better augury for the future."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ae84b26e-6436-352c-9edf-15102c75ff65",
                                        "entry_id": "66e7ea95-5214-3107-8a96-cbc4c4248925",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An event that is experienced as indicating important things to come."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f5debf61-fa70-4bdb-85a1-f28c4cbca3c6",
                                                "sense_id": "ae84b26e-6436-352c-9edf-15102c75ff65",
                                                "text": "Evidently he did not mean to be a mere figurehead, but to carry on the old tradition of Wilsthorpe's; and that was considered to be a good thing in itself and an augury for future prosperity."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "99c5641c-727d-47fb-b7d2-2a0768479373",
                        "source_entry_id": "8ee603f8-65df-388a-9c75-bf83c1e9eb92",
                        "source_sense_id": "036d5148-25b3-3ae1-b07c-92678afcd89b",
                        "target_lang_word": "presage",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "presage",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "037b74ad-f5ea-31a2-bc34-331f136666c5",
                                        "entry_id": "2e361edf-0273-3c4d-bacf-0651dc27d764",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A warning of a future event; an omen."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "229e3ae7-6d0d-4309-93bf-77f333cb0ebd",
                                                "sense_id": "037b74ad-f5ea-31a2-bc34-331f136666c5",
                                                "text": "Speak frankly, Mirzes—nor believe thy words, / Whatever black preſages they contain, / Subjoin'd to all Trophonius hath foretold, / Can change my firm reſolves, or blunt my ſword."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5c3a337f-79ac-3c33-bc43-680ce2ac72e3",
                                        "entry_id": "2e361edf-0273-3c4d-bacf-0651dc27d764",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An intuition of a future event; a presentiment."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e84b528-e74d-43da-9783-c7ae92db5552",
                                                "sense_id": "5c3a337f-79ac-3c33-bc43-680ce2ac72e3",
                                                "text": "Glad was I when I reached the other bank. / Now for a better country. Vain presage!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "presage",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "79e18584-ddcc-3593-8a5e-0274bc83e0da",
                                        "entry_id": "0791061e-b933-3e4c-a0c9-94dccbb81ed0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To predict or foretell something."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d7fc140a-7a8f-4cc6-98be-d13b05caa734",
                                                "sense_id": "79e18584-ddcc-3593-8a5e-0274bc83e0da",
                                                "text": "If I may truſt the flattering truth of ſleepe, / My dreames preſage ſome ioyfull newes at hand : / My boſomes L. ſits lightly in his throne : / And all this day an vnaccuſtom’d ſpirit, / Lifts me aboue the ground with cheatfull thoughts […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e5833c8c-17c4-4cb3-ba72-e21a296e61b7",
                                                "sense_id": "79e18584-ddcc-3593-8a5e-0274bc83e0da",
                                                "text": "That brief moment after the election four years ago, when many Americans thought Mr. Obama’s election would presage a new, less fractious political era, now seems very much a thing of the past."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c0ada764-e142-30ca-be3f-da6d67a9ac31",
                                        "entry_id": "0791061e-b933-3e4c-a0c9-94dccbb81ed0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make a prediction."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
